60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Looking at the options, Option B is the only fiscally responsible choice. It eliminates the high transport costs and the risk of non-refundable deposits associated with whole-building lets. We cannot afford another budget shortfall.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the only logical choice for the organizers. It removes the nightmare of the municipal lottery and the burden of daily cooking duties. We must ensure the staff can actually train, not just manage logistics.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option B is too safe. If members stay separately or commute, we miss the only window for year-groups to actually mix. We risk further isolation and membership loss if we don't prioritize shared living.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I worry that Option C would be too restless. With shared dormitories, we risk the same crowded conditions I found in the inland accounts, which would deprive everyone of the quiet sleep they need to stay focused.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is a financial liability. A guesthouse two prefectures away would maximize transport costs and likely involve the same non-refundable deposits I found in the records. It is an irresponsible choice for the budget.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minako, I understand your concern, but the risk of a deficit is a far more immediate threat to the club's existence. Option B is the only way to guarantee we don't overcharge members or drain the account.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, while I value the social aspect, we cannot ignore the human cost. If we choose Option C, we are signing up for a nine-page application and a lottery. We cannot risk burning out our organizers again.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, @Toshio, the ""human cost"" also includes the members who feel they don't belong and leave the club. Option B fails to address the root cause of our membership loss. We need a shared environment to truly bond.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I understand your heart, but bonding is difficult when people are exhausted. If we choose Option C and the dorms are crowded, the lack of sleep will only lead to irritability and tension, which is the opposite of harmony.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, while I acknowledge the risk of membership loss, Option C is equally problematic. Public facilities often have rigid payment structures, and the shared dorms do not solve the issue of how we handle late cancellations or uneven side-costs. Option B is the most equitable.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minako, we cannot prioritize bonding over solvency. If we choose a distant or rigid option and face another shortfall, the resulting resentment will do more damage to the club's heart than a lack of shared sleeping quarters. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Minako, we cannot build a community on the backs of exhausted organizers. Option C is a logistical disaster, and Option A is too risky. Option B is the only sustainable path that protects our members' time and health. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, @Toshio, I cannot in good conscience vote for a plan that ignores the disintegration of our membership. If we choose Option B, we are merely managing a decline. I believe we must take a risk to save the club's spirit. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I understand your desire to save the club's spirit, but a risk that compromises our rest is too high. Option B allows for a peaceful environment and avoids the chaos of crowded dorms. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, taking a risk with the budget is not the same as saving the club's spirit. Option A's distance and booking terms would likely lead to the very financial unfairness I fear. Option B is the only responsible choice. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"It is clear that the majority of us prioritize stability and sustainability. While I respect Minako's passion, we cannot gamble with the club's finances. Option B is the only rational choice to ensure a fair and solvent camp. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is clear. We must prioritize a system that does not sacrifice the well-being of the organizers for a gamble on social bonding. Option B is the only sustainable decision. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I see that the majority values stability over the social health of the club. While I remain convinced that Option B will not solve our membership crisis, I will not obstruct a unanimous decision. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am glad we have found a path that ensures everyone's peace of mind. By choosing Option B, we protect our rest and our budget, allowing us to focus on the training. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"The decision is logical and fair. By choosing Option B, we eliminate the risk of non-refundable deposits and excessive transport costs, ensuring that no member is unfairly burdened by the actions of others. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
